    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All six final answers are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-73396: R2←R2+2R1 and R3←R3−R1 give rows (1,-1,2,8), (0,0,1,5), and (0,1,-1,1). Swapping the last two rows gives echelon form; back substitution yields z=5, y=6, x=4. The source contains an authored intermediate-matrix typo: immediately before the swap it prints (0,2,-1,1) instead of (0,1,-1,1). Its post-swap matrix and final answer are correct. q-73584: R2←R2+2R1 and R3←R3−3R1, followed by swapping rows 2 and 3, give rows (1,1,-2,3), (0,1,5,-8), and (0,0,1,4). Thus z=4, y=-28, x=39. q-20963: R2←R2−8R1 gives rows (1,2,-1) and (0,0,0), hence x=-1-2y with y arbitrary. q-73740: R2←R2+5R1 gives the same echelon form and general solution. Its source vector notation omits a comma present in the choice; these expressions are equivalent. q-73750: R2←R2+3R1 gives rows (1,-2,4) and (0,0,0), hence x=4+2y with y arbitrary. q-130923: R2←R2+4R1 gives rows (1,-2,-1) and (0,0,3), so the contradiction 0=3 proves there is no solution. The four previously reviewed answers remain unchanged. No submitted grades are supplied; MA evidence comes from captured worked solutions.",
